function lerp(a,b,t){ return a+(b-a)*Math.max(0,Math.min(1,t)); }
// THE ONE SKILL RAMP. UNCHANGED BY THE SIXTY CAP (wave 6, parcel P) — and that is exactly why P is one constant: this law now
// spans 20 -> 60 instead of 20 -> 172, so every consumer compresses onto the reachable mountain with no seam anywhere (it is a
// clamped linear map; moving its endpoint cannot introduce a discontinuity, only re-scale one). CONSEQUENCE, STATED: the expert
// end of every lerp is now genuinely REACHED at the cap rather than approached — measured against the shipped constants,
// bpm 60 goes from dT 0.263 to dT 1.000, which means targetRadius 1.011m -> 0.620m, grooveOpenSec 0.223s -> 0.120s,
// projSpeedNow 39.6 -> 72.0 m/s, spawnMinDeg 22.3deg -> 40.0deg, brownianMax 3.93 -> 11.00, dolly ramp 0.52 -> 1.00, and
// beatQuantDivs 2 steps/beat -> 8. The two beatQuantT thresholds now fall at bpm 36 and bpm 50 (they were 80.8 and 134.0, i.e.
// the 1/4- and 1/8-beat strobes were effectively unreachable). THIS IS INTENDED: 60 is full mastery, not the slow end of
